\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Overview of the one-window delayed-label DASP adaptation cycle. For each current window $W_t$, predictions and MMD evidence are computed before label access and stored in a pending-update queue. At the same outer iteration, labels for $W_{\tau }$, $\tau =t-1$, restore the matching evidence; module-wise gradient conflict and the delayed-label performance holdout then determine repair intensity. The selected localized update is applied directly, unaffected modules remain frozen, and memory, reference, and audit state are updated. The reported primary path does not implement post-update candidate rollback.}}{5}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:window-algorithm}{{1}{5}{Overview of the one-window delayed-label DASP adaptation cycle. For each current window $W_t$, predictions and MMD evidence are computed before label access and stored in a pending-update queue. At the same outer iteration, labels for $W_{\tau }$, $\tau =t-1$, restore the matching evidence; module-wise gradient conflict and the delayed-label performance holdout then determine repair intensity. The selected localized update is applied directly, unaffected modules remain frozen, and memory, reference, and audit state are updated. The reported primary path does not implement post-update candidate rollback}{figure.1}{}}
